          <mxGeometry x="2720" y="1540" width="270" height="245" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="constraints" parent="1" style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=10;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=17;" value="&lt;b&gt;Overall-model constraints&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;O1. User, PlatformRole, AccountStatus, AuthenticatedSession, ActiveContext, PersonalProfile, Club, and ClubRoleAssignment use the canonical shared definitions; module diagrams must not redefine them.&lt;br&gt;O2. Only ACTIVE accounts may perform protected actions. Suspension immediately revokes every current AuthenticatedSession; reactivation never revives an old session.&lt;br&gt;O3. Club authority exists only through current ClubRoleAssignment records. Each non-removed Club has one current administrator assignment, and a User administers at most one Club.&lt;br&gt;O4. A published Announcement belongs to one Club and records the exact current assignment under which it was authored. Published announcements are visible to all users.&lt;br&gt;O5. Connection requester and receiver are distinct. Accepting a Connection does not create a Conversation; the first valid ordinary message creates it atomically. Each accepted unordered pair has at most one direct Conversation with exactly two participants and at least one Message.&lt;br&gt;O6. Per-participant delivery, read, and delete-for-self state is owned by the dedicated chat module. Only a Message sender may delete for everyone, with no current time limit.&lt;br&gt;O7. Administration requires an ACTIVE SYSTEM_ADMIN. Each ModerationAction has exactly one typed target among User, Club, Announcement, Project, and JobPost. Notifications never grant authority, and every administrative state change creates an immutable AuditLog.&lt;br&gt;O8. Project capacity includes the creator. Creation adds one CREATOR ProjectMembership; accepted applications add TEAMMATE memberships atomically while capacity remains. Closing blocks new applications but preserves review of earlier pending applications. Project deletion is soft.&lt;br&gt;O9. Detailed recommendation, mentorship, and career rules remain owned by their module diagrams; this diagram shows only principal cross-module relationships." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="120" y="1930" width="2760" height="360" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="eUserRole" edge="1" parent="1" source="user" target="platformRole" value="uses" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;dashed=1;endArrow=open;fontSize=16;"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="eUserStatus" edge="1" parent="1" source="user" target="accountStatus" value="uses" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;dashed=1;endArrow=open;fontSize=16;"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
